---
// What a Carton boundary holds, as compartments of one box: each is
// separate, and the walls between them are the boundaries.
---

<section class="compartments not-content" aria-labelledby="holds">
  <h2 id="holds">What the boundary holds</h2>
  <div class="box">
    <article>
      <h3>Only exports cross</h3>
      <p>Other Cartons reach what a Carton exports and nothing else: not its top-level constants, its helpers, or the Cartons it imports.</p>
      <pre><code><span class="o"># billing.rb</span>
<span class="c">TAX_RATE</span> = <span class="m">10</span>
<span class="o"># main.rb</span>
<span class="c">TAX_RATE</span>  <span class="x"># NameError</span></code></pre>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Monkey patches stay put</h3>
      <p>A patch to a builtin class, such as ActiveSupport's <code>String#blank?</code>, applies only inside the Carton that makes it.</p>
      <pre><code><span class="o"># billing.rb</span>
<span class="s">''</span>.blank?  <span class="r"># =&gt; true</span>
<span class="o"># main.rb</span>
<span class="s">''</span>.blank?  <span class="x"># NoMethodError</span></code></pre>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Gem versions per Carton</h3>
      <p>Each Carton can set up its own bundle, so two Cartons can load different versions of the same gem in one process.</p>
      <pre><code><span class="o"># billing/Gemfile.lock</span>
bigdecimal (<span class="s">4.1.1</span>)
<span class="o"># shipping/Gemfile.lock</span>
bigdecimal (<span class="s">3.3.1</span>)</code></pre>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .compartments {
    padding-block: 2rem 1rem;
  }

  /* Single column: side margins so the tray never meets the screen edge. */
  @media (max-width: 63.99rem) {
    .compartments {
      padding-inline: clamp(1.25rem, 5vw, 2.5rem);
    }
  }

  h2 {
    margin: 0 0 1.75rem;
    font-size: var(--sl-text-h2);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--sl-color-white);
  }

  /* One ruby-tinted tray, its compartments split by ruby walls. */
  .box {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    border: 1.5px solid var(--carton-tray-edge);
    border-radius: 1.25rem;
    background: var(--carton-tray);
  }

  @media (min-width: 56rem) {
    .box {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }

  article {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    padding: 1.75rem 1.5rem 1.5rem;
  }

  article + article {
    border-top: 1.5px solid var(--carton-tray-edge);
  }

  @media (min-width: 56rem) {
    article + article {
      border-top: 0;
      border-left: 1.5px solid var(--carton-tray-edge);
    }
  }

  h3 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--sl-text-xl);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.014em;
    color: var(--sl-color-white);
  }

  p {
    margin: 0.6rem 0 1.5rem;
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  p code {
    padding: 0.1em 0.3em;
    border-radius: 0.35rem;
    background: var(--carton-ruby-wash);
    color: var(--sl-color-accent-high);
    font-size: 0.86em;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  pre {
    margin: auto 0 0;
    padding: 1rem 1.15rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--carton-line);
    border-radius: 0.9rem;
    background: var(--carton-card);
    box-shadow: var(--carton-shadow);
    font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--code-text);
    overflow-x: auto;
  }

  pre code {
    padding: 0;
    background: none;
    font-size: inherit;
  }

  .c { color: var(--code-constant); }
  .s { color: var(--code-string); }
  .m { color: var(--code-literal); }
  .o { color: var(--code-comment); }
  .r { color: var(--code-result); font-weight: 700; }
  .x { color: var(--code-error); font-weight: 700; }
</style>
